{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Let him complete the evil</b> — it is the verb. <b>And the wicked</b> — they are the objects. And some say: removal of the evil of the wicked." "Rabbi Levi said: for the vav of <b>and who tests hearts and kidneys</b> is superfluous, and its meaning is only: You know who is righteous or wicked. And the meaning of kidneys is a designation for hidden things, like the kidneys, which are hidden. And the meaning of Elohim is righteous is parallel to and You establish the righteous."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:33.286178882Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}